        "id": "s1_parts",
        "kind": "text",
        "label": "The three parts",
        "marks": 1,
        "why": "The word multipolar counts the processes leaving the cell body — many dendrites and one axon — so the name itself gives the plan of the answer.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Writing that a multipolar neuron has many axons. It has many dendrites but only ONE axon.",
          "Naming only two parts. Three are expected."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Multipolar means many poles: many dendrites in, one axon out.",
        "margin_note": "Name the three parts first, then take them in order. Three lines.",
        "mark_note": "Parts",
        "lines": [
          "A multipolar neuron has many dendrites and one",
          "axon arising from the cell body.",
          "These are the commonest neurons of the body.",
          "Its three parts are the dendrites, the cell body",
          "and the axon."
        ]
      },
